# Copy this file to `.env` in the project root, then `flutter run`.
# The build FAILS if .env is missing — that is intentional.
#
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API
#   Project URL        → SUPABASE_URL
#   anon / public key  → SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# ⚠ ON WEB THIS FILE IS PUBLIC.
# flutter_dotenv reads .env as a Flutter asset, so a web build copies it into
# build/web/assets where anyone can download it. That is fine for the anon key
# — it already ships inside every client bundle and row level security is what
# actually protects your data — and it is NOT fine for anything else.
#
# NEVER put here: the service_role key, a database password, or any third-party
# API secret. The app refuses to start if it detects a service_role key, but it
# cannot catch every kind of secret. Real secrets belong in a Supabase Edge
# Function.
#
# Add .env to .gitignore.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
